    {
      "path": "corrected/encode2.c",
      "derived_from": "encode2.c",
      "sha256": "259f1be543de12413da9361de53c2bcc8c1217ced64a759cc67f12b16b074b96",
      "replaced": "(op_mem_idx(op0) << 24)",
      "replacement": "((uint32_t) op_mem_idx(op0) << 24)",
      "occurrences": 1,
      "reason": "enc_rex_mem shifts the unsigned char index register (FE_NOREG = 0x80 for every memory operand without an index) after promotion to int; 128 << 24 overflows int and is undefined behavior in C11, so the pristine encode2.c aborts under -fsanitize=undefined. The unsigned shift produces identical bytes. Used only by the tpde_encodegen_target_x64 generated-consumer sanitizer build; every byte comparison keeps the pristine encode2.c."
    }
